  "id": "attention-decrement",
  "term": "attention decrement",
  "definition": "Attention decrement is a reduction in attentional capacity during a sustained task, meaning a person shifts from full attention to a lower-attention state. In the source, it was indicated by slower reaction times later in the task than earlier.",
